0" :question/problem "$(-63)÷(-9)=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a negative number $(-63)$ by another negative number $(-9).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-63)÷(-9)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $63$ by $9$ without any signs: $63÷9=7.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-63)÷(-9)=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb7c40c9-20df-533c-9bed-9f3d037d2f19"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb7c40c9-20df-533c-9bed-9f3d037d2f19" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7c40c9-20df-533c-9bed-9f3d037d2f19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dd556b47-8cf3-5cfc-bb95-f37a8eafd791" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd556b47-8cf3-5cfc-bb95-f37a8eafd791"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd556b47-8cf3-5cfc-bb95-f37a8eafd791" :answer/id #uuid "dd556b47-8cf3-5cfc-bb95-f37a8eafd791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ece8ebc2-b515-5b96-8b0d-093e31473688" :question/id #uuid "ece8ebc2-b515-5b96-8b0d-093e31473688" :question/math-academy-id "q-99581" :question/problem "Expressed as a fraction, $(-15)÷(-8)=$" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a negative number $(-15)$ by another negative number $(-8).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-15)÷(-8)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $15$ by $8$ without any signs: $15÷8=\\frac{15}{8}.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n(-15)÷(-8)=\\frac{15}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98fe2729-e0b1-5a8f-8618-d765bc69fcc9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98fe2729-e0b1-5a8f-8618-d765bc69fcc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "98fe2729-e0b1-5a8f-8618-d765bc69fcc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8c621007-2cc3-5065-92cc-583010f13ad7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8b8de1b-d772-5cab-b42a-a6f661236480" "answer-eb465cd6-0ae6-5fa7-aee3-eb11355038f1" "answer-a9d3236a-ad9c-5587-8562-492f6fb21edf" "answer-8c621007-2cc3-5065-92cc-583010f13ad7" "answer-fcd2a483-2bae-5502-a39e-7414e8c1db5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8b8de1b-d772-5cab-b42a-a6f661236480" :answer/id #uuid "b8b8de1b-d772-5cab-b42a-a6f661236480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb465cd6-0ae6-5fa7-aee3-eb11355038f1" :answer/id #uuid "eb465cd6-0ae6-5fa7-aee3-eb11355038f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9d3236a-ad9c-5587-8562-492f6fb21edf" :answer/id #uuid "a9d3236a-ad9c-5587-8562-492f6fb21edf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c621007-2cc3-5065-92cc-583010f13ad7" :answer/id #uuid "8c621007-2cc3-5065-92cc-583010f13ad7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcd2a483-2bae-5502-a39e-7414e8c1db5b" :answer/id #uuid "fcd2a483-2bae-5502-a39e-7414e8c1db5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065416 :tutorial/content "Dividing with negative numbers follows similar rules as multiplying with negative numbers. \n\nFirst of all, a negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(+)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let's use this rule to find the value of $(-6) \\div 2.$\n\nHere, since we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-6)$ by a positive number ${\\color{blue}(2)},$ the result is going to be negative:\n![](images/b6/b64108fa03fc286ddcd04ac4cd7a9d77c1672d0ced66ebb1953c97afa5488533.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $6$ by $2$ *without* any signs: $6 \\div 2 = 3.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-6)} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red} -3 }.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065417 :tutorial/content "A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(+)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor instance, to find $8\\div (-2),$ we have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(8)$ by a negative one ${\\color{red}(-2)}.$ So the result will be negative:\n![](images/79/797eda7126fff569fccda2681c628f99f103057d7c5e23c1b65cb566b48ef203.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $8$ by $2$ without any signs: $8 \\div 2 = 4.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}8} \\div {\\color{red}(-2)} = {\\color{red}-4}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065418 :tutorial/content "Finally, the third rule is that a negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(+)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $-12 \\div (-3).$ We have to divide a negative number $\\color{red}(-12)$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-3)}.$ So the result will be positive:\n![](images/d3/d31776de6ab95f8178d0bdd6e3b34cfa2f4fc0b987851dcace50aff1818936da.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $3$ without any signs: $12 \\div 3 = 4.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-12)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue}4}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064421 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
